  "description": "x1 Laurus Nobilis (Bay): Fell to ground level the larger stem to the right hand side and shape round the remaining stem form a much smaller and more manageable size tree. The proposed works form part of routine garden tree management. The Bay has become overgrown for its confined location, with the larger stem leaning onto the boundary fence and contributing to pressure on the structure. Removal of the larger leaning stem will alleviate this pressure, reduce the overall size of the tree and improve its long-term management. The remaining stem will be sympathetically reshaped to create a smaller, balanced and more appropriate specimen for the size of the garden, whilst retaining its amenity value. All works will be carried out in accordance with BS3998:2010 ??? Tree Work ??? Recommendations.",
